{title: When the Saints Go Marching In}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 112}
{meta: public_domain Traditional American spiritual; first published in this form in the early 1900s, from older hymns of the 1890s.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching [C]in,
Oh, when the [C]saints go marching [G]in,
Oh Lord, I [C]want to [C7]be in that [F]number,
When the [C]saints go [G]marching [C]in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh, when the [C]sun refuse to [C]shine,
Oh, when the [C]sun refuse to [G]shine,
Oh Lord, I [C]want to [C7]be in that [F]number,
When the [C]sun re[G]fuse to [C]shine.
{end_of_verse}
